Q: ethersjs disconnects websocker after a while A: <p>It looks like <code>websocket.send(&quot;ping&quot;)</code> may not be doing what you expect here.
Sending <code>&quot;ping&quot;</code> this way is just a text message, not a WebSocket ping frame,
so some RPC providers may ignore it.</p>
<p>This can result in a half-open connection where the socket appears open,
but no events are delivered and no error is emitted.</p>
<p>A more reliable approach is to use an application-level heartbeat (JSON-RPC)
combined with a watchdog:</p>
<ul>
<li>periodically call a cheap RPC method (e.g. <code>eth_blockNumber</code>)</li>
<li>apply a timeout</li>
<li>if it fails or hangs, recreate the provider and re-attach listeners</li>
</ul>
<p>Example (ethers + Nest-style):</p>
<pre class="lang-ts prettyprint-override"><code>
private heartbeatTimer?: NodeJS.Timeout;
private reconnecting = false;

private startHeartbeat() {
  clearInterval(this.heartbeatTimer);

  this.heartbeatTimer = setInterval(async () =&gt; {
    try {
      // &quot;real&quot; liveness check, not a WS ping string
      await this.withTimeout(this.provider.getBlockNumber(), 10_000);
    } catch {
      this.reconnect(&quot;heartbeat failed/hung&quot;);
    }
  }, 30_000);
}
onModuleDestroy() {
  if (this.heartbeatTimer) {
    clearInterval(this.heartbeatTimer);
  }
  const ws = (this.provider as any)?.websocket;
  try { ws?.close(); } catch {}
}
private reconnect(reason: string) {
  if (this.reconnecting) return;
  this.reconnecting = true;

  console.log(`Reconnecting due to: ${reason}`);

  if (this.heartbeatTimer) {
    clearInterval(this.heartbeatTimer);
    this.heartbeatTimer = undefined;
  }

  const ws = (this.provider as any)?.websocket;
  if (ws) {
    try { ws.removeAllListeners(); } catch {}
    try { ws.terminate(); } catch {}
    try { ws.close(); } catch {}
  }

  setTimeout(() =&gt; {
    this.reconnecting = false;
    this.initializeProvider();
    this.startHeartbeat(); // ⚠️ важно!
  }, 1000);
}

private withTimeout&lt;T&gt;(p: Promise&lt;T&gt;, ms: number): Promise&lt;T&gt; {
  return Promise.race([
    p,
    new Promise&lt;T&gt;((_, reject) =&gt; setTimeout(() =&gt; reject(new Error(&quot;timeout&quot;)), ms))
  ]);
}
</code></pre>
